# GRID Layer Model

Read `docs/GRID_LAYER_MODEL.md` before any Studio CMS or content architecture work.

## Mandate

- **Wenige Spiele, maximale Skalierung** — not a Loquiz-style multi-partner platform
- Content = **modular layers** (1=geo, 2=mission, 3=bonus/roles), freely combinable
- **Fixed engine** (Alpha/Beta/Gamma FSM) + variable JSON snapshots

## Before building a Studio feature

Run the checklist in `lib/cms/layer-model.ts` → `LAYER_FEATURE_CHECKLIST`.

If the feature does not serve Layer 1 city scaling, Layer 2 global mission, Layer 3 roles/triggers, or runtime surfaces (outdoor/indoor/online, pulse, language) — **do not build it**.

## Layer mapping

| Layer | Studio field | Runtime |
|-------|--------------|---------|
| 1 Geo | `studio_tasks.layer=1`, GPS / station overrides | `local_waypoints` + `local_stations` |
| 2 Mission | `studio_tasks.layer=2` | `global_levels` (shared across surfaces) |
| 3 Bonus | `studio_tasks.layer=3`, `role_assignment`, `logic_rules` | triggers + roles |

## Play surfaces

outdoor (GPS) · indoor (stations+codes) · online (Tabbrain). Phases: Hub → Quiz → Level → Bonus. Dual fallback via `allowed_fallbacks`. See `lib/grid/play-surface.ts`, `frontend_idee/`.

## Game profiles

Presets: full, city_explorer, indoor_escape, mission/online, micro_pulse.

`studio_games.active_layers` + `runtime_profiles`; event `content_mode` = outdoor | indoor | online.

## Do not prioritize

- Loquiz clone features (Rogain/Open/Match as primary UX) unless runtime engine supports them
- Generic task library features without layer assignment
- Partner self-service game builder
- Checkout/commerce in GRID

## Key paths

- Layer model: `lib/cms/layer-model.ts`
- Surfaces & phases: `lib/grid/play-surface.ts`
- Stations: `lib/grid/stations.ts`, `local_stations`
- Docs: `docs/GRID_LAYER_MODEL.md`
- UI prototype: `frontend_idee/`
- Layer profile UI: `components/cms/games/game-layer-profile-panel.tsx`
